# Jak II: the 30 fps variable jump with presses before the middle sample (init-var-jump's early
# mask), a jump pressed "late" (between the first read and the read again before Jak: one jump),
# then start pressed late (the pause menu opens and stays open: start reaches each pool once).
1000 continue ctysluma-start
1001 -
1002 wait *target* target-stance
1020 wait *target* target-stance
1021 log jump frames 2 press-mid 0 expect level 3
1022 pos *target*
1024 x pos *target*
1025 x pos *target*
1026 pos *target*
1028 pos *target*
1030 pos *target*
1032 pos *target*
1034 pos *target*
1036 pos *target*
1040 pos *target*
1080 wait *target* target-stance
1081 log jump frames 1 press-mid 1 expect level 2
1082 pos *target*
1083 x mid pos *target*
1084 mid pos *target*
1086 pos *target*
1088 pos *target*
1090 pos *target*
1092 pos *target*
1094 pos *target*
1096 pos *target*
1100 pos *target*
1140 wait *target* target-stance
1141 log jump late
1142 pos *target*
1144 x late pos *target*
1145 print *cpad-reread-down*
1146 pos *target*
1148 -
1150 pos *target*
1154 pos *target*
1158 pos *target*
1162 pos *target*
1170 pos *target*
1200 wait *target* target-stance
1201 log start late
1202 start late
1203 print *cpad-reread-down*
1205 -
1210 print *master-mode*
1240 print *master-mode*
1260 start
1262 -
1290 print *master-mode*
1300 log reread end
1302 exit
